Word Scramble

you are running a class and suspect that some of ur students are passing around the answers to mcq disguised as random strings.
Given a list of words and a string , find which word on the list is crambled ip inside the string ,if any . There will be at most one matching word. the lettes dont need to be contiguous.

Question:

your task is to write a function that to find and return the word from the list that si scrambled inside the string, if any exists. If none exists, return result "-" as a string .  
There will be at most one matching word . letters dont need to be in order , letters cant be reused

Code:

import java. util.*;
class main{
    public static void main(String []args){
        String[] words={ "tat" , "dog", "cow" };
        String str ="tdcaowg";
        
        System.out.println(findWord(words, str));
    }
        
        public static String findWord(String[] words, String str){
            // creats a hashmap to store frequency of characters in str
            HashMap<Character , Integer>strMap = new HashMap<>();
            // toCharArray converts string to array of Characters
            for(char ch : str.toCharArray()){
                
                strMap.put(ch, strMap.getOrDefault(ch,0) +1);
            }
               //we check each word
                for(String word : words ){
                // stores frequency of letters in the current word
                HashMap<Character, Integer> wordMap = new HashMap<>();
                
                for(char ch : word.toCharArray()){
                    wordMap.put(ch, wordMap.getOrDefault(ch, 0) +1);
                }
                    Boolean match = true;
                    // gets all the keys
                    for(char ch : wordMap.keySet()){
                        if(strMap.getOrDefault(ch,0)<wordMap.get(ch)){
                            match = false;
                            break;    
                        }    
                    }            
                    
                    if(match){
                        return word;
                    }
                }
        
                 return "-";
        
              }
            }
